                        "name": "Nagavarapu Sai Pavan",
                        "email": "saipavann@ami.com",
                        "username": "saipavann27"
                    },
                    "message": "overall changes are good,It avoids deleting parent interface objects unnecessarily.\n\nI have Below doubt: \n\nIf params.logicalPath == params.ifPath (first time VLAN enable), deconfigureVLAN() is skipped, but later we still create VLAN and reapply saved IP/DHCP/gateway settings.\n\nMy concern is that parent interface settings may remain while the same settings are applied to the new VLAN interface, which can cause duplicate or ambiguous network state.\n\nCan you confirm:\n\n1. How parent interface L3 settings are cleared in this path.\n2. Why this is safe for non-VLAN -> VLAN transition.\n\nNote: Tell me if My understanding is wrong ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "transporthandler.cpp",
                    "line": 631,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "rashidmp",
                        "email": "rashidmp@ami.com",
                        "username": "rashidmp2002"
                    },
                    "message": "This PR's scope is to fix issue https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-networkd/issues/67 by avoiding unnecessary deletion of parent interface objects when configuring VLANs. \n\nThe duplicate behavior you mentioned is existing behavior in current OpenBMC that this PR maintains. The patch adds deconfigureVLAN() to delete only VLAN objects (not parent objects) when changing VLANs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "transporthandler.cpp",
